==Battleground==
*10 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~23.33 seconds<sup>300f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~100 seconds<sup>2,000f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>, delay 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 240 seconds<sup>7,200f</sup>, delay 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 240.33 seconds<sup>7,210f</sup>, delay 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Bore]]s spawn after 300 seconds<sup>9,000f</sup>, delay 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Kory]] spawns after 400 seconds<sup>12,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dancer Cat (Enemy)|Dancer Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
In the beginning, take your time and upgrade your wallet by using Cats with the [[Extra Money]] ability such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]. The stage gets progressively harder the longer you take, but its better to play things passively since Dancer Cat is capable of instantly killing any unit within his range.

[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] do well to handle the Angelic Gories and Metal Doges, while the Dark Otters can be dealt with using [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]. Your goal is to gradually chip down at Dancer Cat with fast units like the aforementioned Maglev Cat and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Bore poses no issue if you bring Courier Cat, and even replenishes your cash every once in a while, since the battle is going to end up being a war of attrition without powerful super-backline [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]]. Kory can pose an issue if you're unprepared, but since there's only one (and at a decently low magnification), a well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can rip a huge chunk off his HP making him far easier to deal with.

This stage will probably end up taking ages, so get ready to be in this for the long haul.

